Repair react-native-ios-utilities 5.2.0's broken publish.

5.2.0 shipped without its build output. The tarball contains no lib/ at all,
while package.json still points main at lib/commonjs/index, module at
lib/module/index and types at lib/typescript/module/src/index.d.ts. For
comparison, 5.1.4 shipped 594 lib/ files including 198 .d.ts declarations.

tsconfig.json maps react-native-ios-context-menu to its raw src/, so tsc type
checks that source, which imports react-native-ios-utilities and hits the
dangling types entry:

    node_modules/react-native-ios-context-menu/src/index.tsx(34,8):
      error TS2307: Cannot find module 'react-native-ios-utilities'
      or its corresponding type declarations.

Seventeen such errors, all in CI. It does not reproduce on a machine with
ignore-scripts=true, because the package expects its prepare script
(react-native-builder-bob) to build lib/ at install time.

Runtime is unaffected either way: the package also sets "react-native":
"src/index", which is the field Metro resolves.

Two changes:

1. Point main, module and types at src/, which is what the tarball actually
   contains.

2. Stop index.ts re-exporting ./example_components/*. Those are demo
   components, unused by this app, and several annotate return types with the
   bare JSX namespace that React 19's types removed in favour of React.JSX --
   six TS2503 errors once the module resolves.

Staying on 5.1.4 is not an option: it hardcodes RCT-Folly 2022.05.16.00, which
React Native 0.85 no longer ships.

Both libraries are due for removal in Phase B, where @expo/ui's MenuView
replaces react-native-ios-context-menu and this patch and 0005 both go away.

